Drop iOS-only global code signing and library validation enforcement options from the macOS
machine configuration so XNU matches Apple's MASTER.arm64.MacOSX behavior:
- Without config_library_validation (CONFIG_ENFORCE_LIBRARY_VALIDATION=0), cs_require_lv()
  honors per-process CS_REQUIRE_LV / Hardened Runtime instead of forcing library validation
  on all processes (including ad-hoc macOS apps loading ad-hoc bundled frameworks).
- Without config_enforce_signed_code (CONFIG_ENFORCE_SIGNED_CODE=0), cs_process_enforcement()
  and csproc_disable_enforcement() follow macOS per-process CS_ENFORCEMENT semantics.
Only the macOS profile applies this patch; iPadOS is unaffected.
